on model is a sharper, more memorable mechanism than X’s broader cost categories.\n\nFor n006, I now see that X’s claim about “next generation of commuters” is confusing and factually off; Y’s cleaner prose avoids this credibility flaw.\n\nI now see that X’s “next generation of commuters” likely refers to commuter e-bikes in bike jargon, so the phrasing is plausible rather than a clarity error. I have also decided X wins on n004 and n002. In n002, X’s “unthought links” insight is sharper and more specific than Y’s vague “integrated wisdom,” and it names clearer triggers for when to compress.\n\nI have decided the winner for n003 is X. The Y candidate contains a disqualifying \"*Draft 2:*\" header.\n\nI have decided the winner for n005 is X. The Y candidate is unreadable.",
